&lt;p&gt;Let&#39;s do something amazing together! The Associate Director, National Accounts will play a critical role in enabling patient access to Arrowhead&#39;s first commercial asset, Redemplo (plozasiran, siRNA targeting APOC3), as well as an expanding pipeline of innovative therapies across multiple therapeutic areas. This product has demonstrated compelling clinical data to date and received approval in November 2025 for the treatment of Familial Chylomicronemia Syndrome (FCS). Redemplo (plozasiran) remains in late-stage development for the treatment of Severe Hypertriglyceridemia (SHTG), with approval anticipated in Q2 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This individual will own a dedicated portfolio of payer and PBM accounts while also serving as a strategic, customer-facing partner to the National Account Directors (NADs) on Arrowhead&#39;s broader national accounts, and as a centralized source of truth for payer contracts, formulary coverage, payer policies, and utilization management criteria across Arrowhead&#39;s U.S. Market Access footprint. The role will translate formulary, claims, and specialty pharmacy data into payer strategy and field-facing insights, partnering closely with the NADs, Trade, Distribution, and Patient Services leadership to strengthen Arrowhead&#39;s payer intelligence capabilities and represent that intelligence directly to internal leadership and external payer and PBM audiences. This is an individual contributor role with no direct reports, requiring high executive presence, polished presentation skills, and the confidence to stand alongside the NADs in front of senior payer and PBM stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a field-based or remote role that requires periodic travel to Arrowhead&#39;s Corporate Headquarters in Pasadena, CA, and to payer and PBM industry conferences, as business needs dictate&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage a dedicated portfolio of payer and PBM accounts, serving as the primary point of contact for day-to-day payer engagement, relationship management, and issue resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support National Account Directors (NADs) on payer and PBM engagements as needed, bringing data-driven insights to the account team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Arrowhead directly with payer and PBM leadership, presenting formulary, policy, and performance insights at business reviews, national conferences, and sales meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend payer and PBM industry conferences alongside NADs and cross-functional leadership to represent Arrowhead&#39;s payer intelligence capabilities and gather market intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the centralized source of truth for payer formulary coverage, published payer policies, and utilization management (UM) criteria, including prior authorization, step therapy, and quantity limit requirements, across Commercial, Medicare Part D, and Medicaid books of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze formularies and policy databases to track payer coverage decisions, formulary tier placement, and UM criteria across assigned payer and PBM accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze pharmacy claims data to identify prior authorization trends, claims patterns, approval and denial rates that signal emerging access barriers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Trade, Distribution, and Patient Services to analyze HUB and specialty pharmacy patient-journey data, translating claims and PA insights into access trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver regular communications to the field on payer coverage wins, policy changes, and key analytical insights to support account and sales team pull-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Market Access, Trade, Distribution, Patient Services, Sales, Commercial Analytics, and Finance to address payer access challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure full compliance with US healthcare regulations, legal standards, and corporate policies in all analyses and communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
