&lt;p&gt;The Executive Director, Strategic Operations is essential for steering Arrowhead’s strategic planning and operational excellence to ensure the seamless execution of our Global Operations and Product Delivery. As the Strategy and Operations Leader, you will play a vital role in facilitating the alignment and governance of Arrowhead’s technical portfolio, so we can achieve business agility. You will be responsible for the refinement and prioritization of our portfolio, developing our functional operating rhythm, and ensuring cross-functional alignment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in Pasadena, California, with an expectation to be in office 5 days a week. This position is posted at the Executive Director level; however, depending on the selected candidate’s experience and qualifications, the role may be filled at the Senior Director level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Portfolio Management&lt;/strong&gt; Facilitate the refinement and prioritization of the technical portfolio backlog, ensuring strategic alignment and optimal resource allocation. This role ensures our product and work package teams are in a constant state of readiness to anticipate and act on external changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Management&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and manage functional operating rhythm to enhance organizational efficiency and effectiveness. Lead operational reviews and ensure execution against strategic plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Long Range Planning &lt;/strong&gt;Lead strategic planning for lifecycle management (LCM) across the Global Operations and Product Delivery portfolio with focus on maximizing the long-term value of our assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trade Operations &lt;/strong&gt;Oversee the global trade policy and strategy direction, drive proactive regulatory engagement, and partner with senior and executive leadership across Supply Chain, Commercial, Legal, Finance, Tax, Regulatory, and Quality to align trade compliance strategies with business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Functional Alignment&lt;/strong&gt; Foster alignment and integration across teams ensuring proactive collaboration and cohesion in achieving strategic goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk Management and Network Strategy &lt;/strong&gt;Develop critical manufacturing strategies and plans identifying operational factors that impact capacity and network limits. Recommend strategies supporting business case development and investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance Process &lt;/strong&gt;Play an integral role in the governance process for the technical portfolio, including partnerships and licensees requiring Arrowhead CMC or Supply services, ensuring that decisions are made transparently and effectively. The Governance team will understand the financial, technical, and business contexts &amp;amp; hold strategy and investment funding responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluation and Assessment&lt;/strong&gt; Support and/or lead strategic evaluations and initiatives that inform PT and assessments; what are competitive levers now &amp;amp; future; what are current gaps in technology and portfolio mix; identification of emerging areas of unmet needs, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transformation &amp;amp; Change Management&lt;/strong&gt; Champion organizational change management initiatives, particularly those related to the integration of advanced technologies, fostering a culture of innovation and adaptability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget and Metrics&lt;/strong&gt; Own the budget and develop organizational metrics that track and measure the success of strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supplier / Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt; Support and/or lead the process by which the Global Operations organization manages suppliers and partnerships to ensure favorable terms and performance in line with company objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Initiatives&lt;/strong&gt; Advocate for key talent initiatives, nurturing an environment of diversity, inclusion, and belonging. Promote talent development opportunities, internship programs, and other initiatives that support workforce excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal Communications&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with corporate affairs to ensure clear and consistent communication across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Doctorate degree &amp;amp; 6 years of strategic planning and operational experience OR&amp;nbsp; Master’s degree &amp;amp; 10 years of strategic planning and operational experience OR&amp;nbsp;Bachelor’s degree &amp;amp; 12 years of strategic planning and operational experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 years of managerial experience directly managing people and/or leadership experience leading teams, projects, programs or directing the allocation of resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership and communication skills; effective vendor management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively in a matrixed, team-based environment, with strong organizational and time management capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You may be required to travel for up to 20% of your time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
