&lt;p&gt;Let’s do something amazing together! The National Account Director (NAD) will play a critical role in enabling patient access to Arrowhead’s first commercial asset – Redemplo (plozasiran, siRNA targeting APOC3) as well as an expanding pipeline of innovative therapies across multiple therapeutic areas. This product has demonstrated compelling clinical data to date and received approval in November 2025 for the treatment of Familial Chylomicronemia Syndrome (FCS). Redemplo (plozasiran) remains in late-stage development for the treatment of Severe Hypertriglyceridemia (SHTG).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The NAD will develop, execute, and manage strategic relationships with key government stakeholders, including Managed Medicaid, Fee-for-Service Medicaid, the Department of Veterans Affairs, DoD/TRICARE, Indian Health Service, and Humana Medicare, to secure formulary and coverage access. The ideal candidate will demonstrate strong individual account management skills and the ability to influence cross-functionally to support Arrowhead’s expanding commercial portfolio. This is a field-based role that requires periodic travel to Arrowhead&#39;s Corporate Headquarters in Pasadena, CA, as business needs dictate.&lt;/p&gt;
