&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen relationships with key government accounts, including Managed Medicaid, Fee-for-Service Medicaid, the Department of Veterans Affairs, DoD/TRICARE, Indian Health Service, and Humana Medicare&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate product clinical and economic value to payers, and key decision-makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain comprehensive account plans supporting launch, and post-launch strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead contract negotiations, evaluate performance metrics, and ensure organizational alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop the organizational structure and capabilities required to support effective payer engagement across the expanding U.S. Arrowhead portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor sales implications for each payer negotiation and take action to establish optimal access in the right direction as necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams, including Sales, Medical Affairs, Commercial Analytics, Finance, and Compliance, to address access challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide market intelligence updates on payer trends, coverage determinations, and healthcare policy changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present payer policy insights at internal business reviews, national conferences, and sales meetings to align strategic priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure full compliance with US healthcare regulations, legal standards, and corporate policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
