&lt;p&gt;This position plays a key role in scaling Arrowhead’s partnership operations from early clinical supply through commercial launch and lifecycle management, ensuring contractual compliance, forecast accuracy, supply continuity, and cost-effective execution while supporting global regulatory filings across multiple health authorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership Supply Chain Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary supply chain point of accountability and liaison for Arrowhead’s partner-facing supply activities, including current partnerships such as Takeda, GSK, and Sarepta, Novartis, as well as additional current and future regional and global collaborations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Arrowhead Supply Chain in Joint Manufacturing Committees, Joint Operating Committees, and supply working group forums with each partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate partnership contracts (Supply Agreements, Quality Agreements, Clinical Supply Agreements, CSAs) into operational plans, SoWs, SOPs, and KPIs, ensuring Arrowhead meets all contractual obligations including lead times, forecast accuracy, allocation rules, and service levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain trusted, transparent working relationships with counterpart supply chain, regulatory, and quality leaders at each partner organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demand &amp;amp; Supply Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the integrated S&amp;amp;OP process for partner products, consolidating partner forecasts and incorporate into Arrowhead’s global supply plan and reconciling against drug substance and drug product capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead demand reviews with each partner, challenge forecast assumptions, and ensure forecast quality meets defined accuracy and bias targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical &amp;amp; Commercial Supply Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and communicate the end-to-end order-to-delivery process for clinical through commercial supply shipments to partners, including order confirmation, release coordination, customs documentation, and on-time delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cold-chain logistics, importation, customs clearance, and in-country distribution coordination into partner markets, working with qualified 3PLs and freight forwarders, as applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory &amp;amp; Quality Interface&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Regulatory Affairs to align supply activities with partner-territory filings, post-approval changes, and license maintenance across multiple health authorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Quality Assurance on partner Quality Agreements, batch disposition for partner markets, deviation/CAPA communications, and complaint handling supply implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support technology transfer activities into partner-affiliated or partner-managed manufacturing nodes where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional &amp;amp; Strategic Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Supply Chain in alliance governance and contribute to negotiation of amendments, change orders, and new supply terms for current and prospective partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and report supply chain KPIs (OTIF, forecast accuracy, inventory DOH, partner satisfaction) to internal and external leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and mitigate supply chain risks specific to partner operations (geopolitical, regulatory, logistics, single-source dependencies) and own associated business continuity plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead continuous improvement initiatives to scale partnership supply chain operations as Arrowhead’s pipeline and partnership portfolio expand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Technical Operations, CMC, Manufacturing, Quality, Regulatory, Legal, Alliance Management, and Finance to deliver integrated outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
