&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. in Supply Chain, Engineering, Life Sciences, Business, or related discipline. Advanced degree (M.B.A., M.S., or relevant scientific field) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of progressive pharmaceutical or biotech supply chain experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in a partnership, alliance, or external supply role with direct partner-facing accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing clinical and/or commercial supply into out-licensed or co-development partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of GxP, ICH guidelines, and pharmaceutical Quality Agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage complex S&amp;amp;OP processes and interface with external partners on demand forecasts and supply commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP systems and demand planning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills; ability to navigate cultural and time-zone differences across global partner organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of FDA, EMA, and ICH GMP requirements; familiarity with additional health authority requirements (PMDA, NMPA, MHRA, etc.) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APICS CPIM/CSCP or equivalent supply chain certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience supporting partnerships with large global pharma (e.g., Takeda, GSK, Sarepta, Novartis, or comparable organizations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RNAi, oligonucleotide, gene therapy, or other novel modality supply chains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to lead and coordinate large, complex strategy projects with minimal direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing operations network strategies for a growing global market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnership mindset — comfortable representing Arrowhead externally while protecting Arrowhead’s commercial and operational interests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-cultural fluency — operates effectively across diverse global business norms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems thinker — connects upstream CMC and manufacturing constraints to downstream partner commercial needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with biologics, oligonucleotides, or other temperature-controlled (cold-chain, 2–8 °C or frozen) products.&lt;/li&gt;
