&lt;p&gt;The Research Technician I provides daily husbandry support for our AAALAC accredited San Diego vivarium. Daily husbandry support includes morning and afternoon cage-side health observations for the mice and rats, bi-weekly cage changes, animal receiving and ear tagging, and general room upkeep. Additional duties include various vivarium sanitation tasks, such as cleaning cage equipment, sanitizing procedure and storage rooms, inventory and supply management, and other duties as assigned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is onsite 5 days a week in San Diego.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs animal health checks which may include performing post dose observations and documents study related health changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs sanitation of vivarium&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs routine cage changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs routine animal colony health surveillance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs general husbandry duties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs animal receiving
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Housing&lt;/li&gt;
