&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals is seeking a Senior Contracts Analyst to join its Legal Team in Pasadena, California. Reporting to Arrowhead’s Contracts Manager, the Senior Contracts Analyst will be responsible for evaluating, drafting, negotiating, and managing a broad range of company contracts on behalf of Arrowhead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate will have strong writing and negotiation skills, excellent attention to detail, sound judgment, and the ability to assess contractual risk independently. This individual should be responsive, tech savvy, comfortable working across multiple priorities, and able to understand how contracting decisions support Arrowhead’s broader business objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;This role requires someone who can operate effectively in a fast-paced environment where contracts must be negotiated accurately, efficiently, and with appropriate consideration of legal and business risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Candidates should have 3+ years of contract negotiation and contract management experience, preferably within the biotechnology or pharmaceutical industry, with a strong understanding of a variety of commercial and business contract types and the ability to quickly identify and assess key contractual risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is full-time and onsite five days per week in Pasadena, California.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review, negotiate, evaluate, and execute a broad range of contract documents, ensuring appropriate terms, timelines, deliverables, and alignment with Arrowhead’s risk parameters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify contractual provisions that may present legal, financial, operational, or business risk and work with internal stakeholders to resolve or mitigate concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage a high volume of agreements while maintaining accuracy, responsiveness, and appropriate prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accurate and timely entry and maintenance of contract data within Arrowhead’s contract management system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate directly with internal and external stakeholders regarding contractual matters and negotiation status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance, Procurement, and business teams to understand objectives and develop contract solutions that appropriately balance business needs and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare, revise, and manage amendments, termination notices, statements of work, and other contractual correspondence and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply established contracting standards, templates, and fallback positions while exercising sound judgment when escalation is appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support contract lifecycle management processes and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with other general legal and contracting matters, as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance broader business considerations with day-to-day contracting priorities and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of contract negotiation and contract management experience, including experience independently managing a high volume of agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience drafting and negotiating a variety of contract types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of contractual terms, risk assessment, and negotiation principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills with strong attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, critical-thinking, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to assess risk and make sound recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and exercise judgment within established contracting guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with internal clients and cross-functional teams to understand business objectives and develop practical contract solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to manage multiple agreements, deadlines, and stakeholders simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, regulated environment&lt;/li&gt;
