&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The Tax Manager will oversee the company’s tax compliance, reporting, and strategic tax planning activities. This role is responsible for managing global tax provision work, corporate income tax filings, indirect tax matters, tax audits, internal controls, and relationships with external tax advisors. The Tax Manager will partner cross-functionally with Finance, Accounting, Legal, and external service providers to ensure accurate and timely tax reporting, compliance with applicable regulations, and effective support of business initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires strong technical tax knowledge, attention to detail, sound judgment, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a growing, fast-paced organization. The ideal candidate is hands-on, collaborative, analytical, and comfortable both leading tax-related projects and executing detailed tax work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in Pasadena or San Diego, CA with an expectation to be in office 5 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
